cast_shell: fix the label for the v4l2 decode-accelerator test target

The cast test list reaches for //media/gpu:video_decode_accelerator_tests,
but that test is declared in media/gpu/test/BUILD.gn, so the label it wants
is //media/gpu/test:video_decode_accelerator_tests - which is exactly what
the root BUILD.gn uses for the same target. gn resolves the whole build
graph even when only cast_shell is being built, so the stale label fails
`gn gen` outright with "Unresolved dependencies" and nothing compiles.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Joey Eamigh <55670930+JoeyEamigh@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/chromecast/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chromecast/BUILD.gn
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@
   }
 
   if (use_v4l2_codec) {
-    tests += [ "//media/gpu:video_decode_accelerator_tests" ]
+    tests += [ "//media/gpu/test:video_decode_accelerator_tests" ]
   }
 
   if (is_linux) {
